            <ArticleTitle>Patient controlled analgesia for the young pediatric patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>251-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A collaborative effort to improve pain control in the young pediatric patient resulted in new policies and a change in pain management practice. A retrospective chart review of 15 pediatric surgical patients identified the use of patient controlled analgesia (PCA) as a successful method of pain control for children 3 years of age and older.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
